<office:body><office:text>
 <text:tracked-changes>
  <text:changed-region text:id="ct1"><text:insertion><office:change-info><dc:creator>Reviewer One</dc:creator><dc:date>2026-08-01T10:00:00</dc:date></office:change-info></text:insertion></text:changed-region>
  <text:changed-region text:id="ct2"><text:deletion><office:change-info><dc:creator>Reviewer Two</dc:creator><dc:date>2026-08-02T11:00:00</dc:date></office:change-info><text:p>seven </text:p></text:deletion></text:changed-region>
 </text:tracked-changes>
 <text:table-of-content text:name="TOC1"><text:table-of-content-source text:outline-level="2"><text:index-title-template>Contents</text:index-title-template></text:table-of-content-source><text:index-body><text:index-title text:name="t"><text:p>Contents</text:p></text:index-title><text:p>1. Purpose 1</text:p><text:p>2. Retention schedule 1</text:p></text:index-body></text:table-of-content>
 <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1">Purpose</text:h>
 <text:p text:style-name="Standard">This policy sets out how long records are kept<text:note text:id="ftn1" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>1</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p>Records includes paper, electronic and recorded media.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note> and who may destroy them. A <text:span text:style-name="Defined">Record Owner</text:span> is accountable for each class. See <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://standards.example.invalid/retention">the retention standard</text:a> and <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="sched">the schedule below</text:bookmark-ref>.<office:annotation office:name="c1"><dc:creator>Legal Reviewer</dc:creator><dc:date>2026-08-03T09:30:00</dc:date><text:p>Should this cite the statutory minimum?</text:p></office:annotation> Exceptions need <text:span text:style-name="T_hl">written approval</text:span> and are <text:span text:style-name="T_du">never</text:span> implied.</text:p>
 <text:p text:style-name="Standard">Financial records are kept for <text:change-start text:change-id="ct1"/>ten <text:change-end text:change-id="ct1"/><text:change text:change-id="ct2"/>years from the end of the financial year.</text:p>
 <text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="Frame" draw:name="Callout" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="5cm" svg:height="2.2cm"><draw:text-box><text:p>CALLOUT: legal hold overrides every period in this policy.</text:p></draw:text-box></draw:frame>When litigation is reasonably anticipated, destruction stops at once for the affected classes, and resumes only on written release.</text:p>
 <text:p text:style-name="PolicyClause">1.1 A clause in the house style, hanging indent, justified, italic from its style.</text:p>
 <text:list text:style-name="Clauses"><text:list-item><text:p>Identify the record class.</text:p><text:list><text:list-item><text:p>Check the statutory minimum.</text:p><text:list><text:list-item><text:p>Record the source of the minimum.</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p>Check the business need.</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p>Apply the longer of the two.</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p>Log the decision.</text:p></text:list-item></text:list>
 <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="sched"/>Retention schedule</text:h>
 <table:table table:name="Schedule" table:style-name="Tbl"><table:table-column table:number-columns-repeated="4"/>
  <table:table-header-rows><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="CellHead"><text:p><text:span text:style-name="T_white">Class</text:span></text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="CellHead"><text:p><text:span text:style-name="T_white">Owner</text:span></text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="CellHead" table:number-columns-spanned="2"><text:p><text:span text:style-name="T_white">Period and trigger</text:span></text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row></table:table-header-rows>
  <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell" table:number-rows-spanned="2"><text:p>Finance</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>Controller</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="CellAmber"><text:p>10 years</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>End of financial year</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
  <table:table-row><table:covered-table-cell/><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>Tax lead</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>7 years</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>Filing date</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
  <table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>People</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>HR director</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>6 years</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Cell"><text:p>Leaving date</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row>
 </table:table>
 <text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Two-column guidance</text:h>
 <text:section text:style-name="TwoCol" text:name="Cols"><text:p text:style-name="Standard">COLUMN-TEXT-START The left column carries guidance for record owners, who review their classes each year and confirm the periods still hold.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Standard">The right column carries guidance for everyone else, who must not destroy a record outside the schedule. COLUMN-TEXT-END</text:p></text:section>
 <text:p text:style-name="Standard">AFTER-COLUMNS the document returns to one column. Date printed: <text:date text:date-value="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</text:date>.</text:p>
</office:text></office:body></office:document>
